cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this library in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "stm32-st7789-gfx: a portable, host-testable C graphics library for ST7789 displays on STM32"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Pastrana"
    given-names: "Juan"
    alias: "JuanP-G"
repository-code: "https://github.com/JuanP-G/stm32-st7789-gfx"
url: "https://juanp-g.github.io/stm32-st7789-gfx/"
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-29"
keywords:
  - STM32
  - ST7789
  - FMC
  - RGB565
  - embedded GUI
  - anti-aliased fonts
  - host-testable
abstract: >-
  Portable C99 graphics library for ST7789 panels on STM32 microcontrollers
  (16-bit parallel FMC, RGB565, 240 x 240): shapes, anti-aliased text, icons,
  images and widgets. It paints through an address window and a pixel burst,
  uses integer arithmetic only, and talks to the hardware through two
  functions. Every drawing path is tested on a PC against a controller model.
